## [ENT-187] | 2026-11-18 00:17 UTC | Apollo | general | ref: game/fleet/route_run.py | see: orders.log ENT-052
Three new stop fields of the circuit runner, for every division (commit 85b14c83, installed through fleet-build.sh; six tests in scripts/tests/test_fleet_route_run.py failed on the old runner and pass now, the whole suite passed in the install):
- `bunker: {"keep": N}` at an outpost of ours: the fuel cells aboard are burnt into the tank by whole cells (one `refuel` call with item_id fuel_cell and a quantity, never more cells than the tank's room / 20), the tank above N is deposited into the faction's fuel reserve (`deposit` item_id fuel, target faction), turn by turn until no cell is left; a refused deposit ends the step; the run row notes the fuel moved and the reserve read after.
- `burn_cells: true`: the cells aboard go into the tank, as many whole cells as its room takes (a cell is 100 cr for 20 fuel at The Experiment and Central Nexus, about 5 cr a unit, where station fuel costs 11 to 15 cr a unit).
- `refuel: false`: the stop docks without the station's fuel (default true, as before). Every route flies as before unless it names one of the three.
- First user: supply-bunker-gsc-0044 (65 cells from The Experiment into the bunker of CLTV Outpost GSC-0044, keep 30; three runs in all as a budget, members only). The bunker read 1,258 of 50,000 at 23:52 UTC.
- The fields are in game/routes/BLUEPRINT.md, table "A stop of a circuit". @Unity: requests.log ENT-251 and ENT-255 (3) asked for the bunker and the burn as runner steps.

